<title>USA: Aftermarket Technology sets IPO terms.</title>
<headline>Aftermarket Technology sets IPO terms.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aftermarket Technology Corp will offer 3.5 million shares in its planned initial public offering for about $12.50 to $14.50 a share, according to regulatory documents.</p>
<p>When the company first filed for a proposed IPO in June, it did not include any terms. Lead underwriter Morgan Stanley said deal is tentatively slated for December.</p>
<p>The company makes drive train products used in repairing cars and light trucks.</p>
